hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2789","###
 Narrated to us Yunus bin Abd al-A'la, who informed us that Ibn Wahb reported, stating that Malik informed him. [In another chain]: Narrated to us Al-Fadl bin Ya'qub, who narrated that Muhammad bin Ja'far narrated, who narrated that Malik bin Anas narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aisha (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever has the sacrificial animal (Hady) with him,"
"2790","Narrated to us 'Abdah ibn 'Abdullah al-Khuza'i, who informed us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Bishr al-'Abdi, on the authority of Muhammad, who is Ibn 'Umar, on the authority of Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah (RA), who said: ""We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for Hajj in three states: some of us entered the state of Ihram for both Hajj and 'Umrah together (Q"
